Patch 63 -- route every audited indirect call in entry 34's closure.

This is the patch that made entry 34 run. It has two halves, developed together:
the format converters that the last device fault named, and the 37 further calls
a static audit found before the next launch instead of after it.

## Why an audit and not another launch

Every island wall so far has been the same defect: a function pointer read out of
a GUEST WineD3D object and called directly, so native ARM branches into i386
bytes. Each was found by launching, faulting, and looking up an address:

```text
fbo_ops and plain gl_ops calls        patch 61
glDrawBuffer, absent from this stack  patch 62
format->upload / ->download          this patch, first half
```

`harness/island/full/island_icall_audit.py` finds them statically instead. For the
closure of one entry it lists every call through a function-pointer FIELD and
splits routed from unrouted. On entry 34:

```text
closure                          432 functions
function-pointer field names     117 (from the module's own headers)
UNROUTED indirect calls           47
  of those, real calls            39   routed by this patch (two by the first half)
  pointer tests and declarations   8   nothing to route
```

Two of its own bugs were found and fixed while it was being written, both of the
kind that produce a confident empty answer: `__attribute__((noinline))` was taken
for a function definition and swallowed the real one below it -- which hid
`wined3d_texture_load_location` itself -- and the member-call pattern required
`->name(`, which never matches a site already wrapped as
`MGS2_P50_CALL(site, x->name)(...)`, so both the routed sites and the ops targets
behind them were invisible. Its control check (the closure must contain at least
one ROUTED call) is what caught the second one.

## What is routed, by family

`MGS2_P50_CALL()` already existed for this: it wraps the POINTER expression, so
the argument list and return value are untouched, and it is the identity macro
unless MGS2_ISLAND_ARM is defined. One id per family rather than 39 ids -- the
abort in `mgs2_island_dispatch()` prints the guest pointer, which identifies the
exact target through the class-B table, so per-site numbering would buy nothing:

```text
23/24  FORMAT_UPLOAD / FORMAT_DOWNLOAD   texture_gl.c, the converters the device
                                          fault named: convert_b8g8r8a8_unorm_gles
25     FORMAT_DECOMPRESS                  the third member of the same triple,
                                          which the audit found and a launch had not
26     BLITTER_BLIT                  7    blitter chains, texture_gl/surface/texture_vk
27     BLITTER_DESTROY               6
28     CONTEXT_OPS                   6    cs.c submit/finish/require_space/
                                          reference_resource/map_upload_bo
29     TEXTURE_UPLOAD_CPU            2    surface.c CPU blit uploads
30     ADAPTER_OPS                  12    adapter create/destroy across the module
31     MISC_OPS                      5    allocator chunks, context-data frees,
                                          swapchain_frontbuffer_updated
```

Site ids are declared at the END of `wined3d_private.h`, not next to sites 0-22:
adding lines above line 4115 would move the `assert()` line numbers that the
shipping DLL bakes into its own code. No call site gained a line either, for the
same reason.

Fail-closed is inherited, not re-implemented: `mgs2_island_dispatch()` aborts when
it cannot map a pointer, in every build, so a routed call that turns out to
target something unmappable stops legibly instead of executing i386 bytes.

## Verification

`MGS2_P50_CALL(site, fp)` is `(fp)` in the guest build, so the shipping DLL must
not change. All 32 wined3d translation units compiled for i386 before and after,
from the same source path: `.text`, `.rdata` and `.data` byte-identical in every
one. Eleven objects differ in DWARF only, because the wrapped expressions moved
source columns.

## Result on the device

Entry 34 armed, 18 entries, production DLL pair:

```text
4200+ frames through the whole attract demo, its death and the MISSION FAILED menu
zero island faults, zero traps, zero unresolved dispatches
screenshot shows correct rendering
```

Also verified on a timing-capable build with MGS2_ISLAND_DIAGNOSTICS off
(`box86-island41`, 02294e0fc53298e9fc02c50ff5a5aa10392e44e78619358359fb6a172d104b71):
1800 frames, 18 entries armed, no faults.

NOT MEASURED. No frame-rate claim: attract mode cannot measure these entries -- 3
of 9 A/B cycles balanced, all in the capped window. The measurement needs the
owner's save and about 20 minutes of real gameplay.

